# Sandbender Scavengers {W}{B}, 1/1: "Whenever you sacrifice another permanent, put a +1/+1 counter on this creature." and "When this creature dies, you may exile it. When you do, return target
# creature card with mana value less than or equal to this creature's power from your graveyard to the battlefield." Bot1 sacrifices a Lotus Petal (2/2), then Bot2's Lightning Bolt kills the Scavengers
# (it ends in exile, accepted). The reflexive ability can't target Hill Giant (mana value 3 > 2), a Lotus Petal (no creature) or Bot2's Memnite (not from your graveyard), so Grizzly Bears
# (mana value 2, equal to the power) is its only legal target and is chosen for Bot1 (a prompt would be left unanswered if another card were legal). Bot2's own Lightning Bolt first kills its own Memnite, so Bot2's graveyard holds a creature card that stays put.

